From 18355f97568ac2a35a9161149ed1ea7d1525e6bb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yvan Janssens <yvanj@cyber.gent>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 12:40:14 +0100
Subject: [RFC PATCH 7/7] KVM: s390: selftests: Add a test for the
 ESA/390-compatibility mode

Run a small ESA/390 program without dynamic address translation in a VM
with KVM_CAP_S390_ESA390_CM and check, with one and with two vCPUs:

- the capability and the attribute are refused when they cannot be used;
- interruptions the machine presents (supervisor call, the specification
  exception for a PSW with the DAT bit) and the ones KVM presents
  (operation exception, injected program interruption, restart, external,
  input/output, machine check) use the eight-byte PSWs and the ESA/390
  locations, in the prefix area of the CPU, and leave the z/Architecture
  PSW locations alone;
- the PSW is exchanged with user space in the 16-byte format;
- a prefix area of 4K bytes is used, and the prefix is aligned to 8K when
  the configuration leaves the mode;
- SIGP external call and emergency signal reach a second CPU, sense
  running status is an invalid order, set architecture comes to user
  space;
- the switch to z/Architecture and back;
- facility bit 2 is zero in the mode and one in z/Architecture mode, in
  KVM_S390_VM_CPU_PROCESSOR and for STORE FACILITY LIST (EXTENDED) in the
  guest, while bits 138 and 168 stay as user space set them;
- guest debugging cannot be enabled in the mode, and the mode cannot be
  entered while it is enabled.

The checks that need no guest to run (interface, facility list, guest
debugging) also run on a host that refuses ESA/390-format state
descriptions; the test skips the rest there.

The address of the second prefix area can be given as an argument.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-fable-5-2
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
---
